Step 1: Decide what we want
We want:
A page to create quiz questions
Each question:
Has a number (Question 1, 2, 3…)
Has an input box
A button to add more questions dynamically


So we need:
HTML → structure
CSS → optional styling
JavaScript → logic & interaction


Step 2: Create the static HTML structure
 visible part:
<h2>Create Quiz Questions</h2>
<div id="questionContainer"></div>
<button id="addQuestionBtn">AddQuestion</button>

Why h2 , div  and button :-

h2 → heading
div → empty container where questions will be inserted
button → user interaction

Step 3: Track how many questions exist

We need automatic numbering, so we create a counter:

let qCounter = 0;


Step 4: Create a reusable function
function createQuestionCard(prefill) { ... }

Why

We need to create question cards:

On page load
On button click
One function = reusable logic


Step 5: Build the question card inside the function

Increase counter
qCounter++;        So each card gets a new number.


create a div (question card)

const qDiv = document.createElement('div');

This creates:
<div></div>

Add a CSS class

qDiv.className = 'question-card';
So CSS can style it later.

Decide input value

const questionText = prefill ? prefill.text : '';

If data is provided → use it
Otherwise → empty input


qDiv.innerHTML = `
  <strong>Question ${qCounter}:</strong>
  <input type="text" value="${questionText}">
`;


This:
Adds dynamic question number
Creates an input field


Return the element
return qDiv;
So we can insert it into the page.




PART 2: Flow of EXECUTION (what the browser does)
tep 1: Browser loads HTML
Shows heading
Shows button
Container is empty

Step 2: Browser reaches <script>
JavaScript starts running top to bottom.

Step 3: Function is defined

function createQuestionCard(prefill) { ... }


Step 4: Container is selected

const container = document.getElementById('questionContainer');

Now JS knows where to add questions.


Step 5: Event listener is attached
addEventListener('click', () => {...});

This means:
“When the button is clicked, run this code.”

Step 6: First question is created automatically

const firstCard = createQuestionCard({ text: "What is Javascript?" });

So Question 1 appears immediately.

Step 7: User clicks the button 
each click:
1. Calls createQuestionCard()
2. increments counter 
3. Creates a new card
4. Appends it to the container

















